Projects group cards, decisions and notes. A project has a visibility (org:
everyone in the org can read it; private: only its members and org admins), a
lease (how long a claim lives without renewal) and per-project members.

Examples:
  lorvik project ls
  lorvik project create payments --name "Payments" --visibility private --lease 1h
  lorvik project member add 106666050296328877 --role member -p payments
  lorvik project archive payments

Usage
  lorvik project [flags]
  lorvik project [command]

Commands
  archive     Archive a project (or restore it with --undo)
  create      Create a project
  edit        Change a project's name, description, visibility, concurrency or lease
  ls          List the projects you can see
  member      List and manage a project's members
  show        Show a project with its card counts

Flags
  -h, --help   help for project

Global flags
      --api-url string   Server URL (default: LORVIK_API_URL)
      --json             Output the raw API JSON
  -p, --project string   Project slug (default: LORVIK_PROJECT or .lorvik.toml)
  -Q, --quiet            Suppress the unread notice on stderr and an empty inbox
      --session string   Session label for this chat (default: LORVIK_SESSION or derived; see lorvik session)

Run 'lorvik project <command> --help' for more information about a command.
